# The image is built from a clean checkout in CI, but a local `docker build .`
# hands Docker whatever the working tree holds. Two kinds of leftovers matter.
#
# A symlink breaks the build outright: `pub` points at a checkout elsewhere on
# the developer's disk, and once it is inside the image, Node resolves modules
# along a path that does not exist in the container. The publisher then cannot
# find its own dependencies, while `/app/node_modules` sits there untouched.
# Measured 2026-09-25: the same export succeeded on the published image and
# failed on a locally built one for this reason alone.
#
# The rest only make the image fat — 2.82 GB against the published 2.38 GB.
node_modules
pub
pub.demo
.mounts
.next
out
built
public/*
.yarn/cache
.yarn/install-state.gz
*.tsbuildinfo
